                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238957248",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197982796274",
                            "num_reviews": 40,
                            "playtime_forever": 785,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 357,
                            "playtime_at_review": 639,
                            "last_played": 1793663244
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolute classic. Graphics are very dated, but in a way also very pure, in that you get no distracting anomalies and the game runs very smoothly, even using the VR mod. If you are struggling against the AI, which are quite nippy, just increase the AIRange value in the track's AIW file to say 0.5. If you go too high some of the AI will behave quite strange. What this value does (in brief) is define how much influence the Speed parameters have in .rcd files, but only for that track. Also if you have a Logitech G29 wheel, GHub is bugged and keeps the wheel centre strength on during racing in this game. This makes the wheel feel very heavy. You can install the earlier (pre-GHub) drivers: LGS_9.04.49_x64_Logitech.exe. But I found a better workaround. Just create an AMS1 profile in GHub only for when you play this game. Make it persistent while you play this game. Then set 'Centering Spring in Non Force Feedback Games' to checked and set the 'Centering Spring Strength' to 1 (not 0 or 20, that won't work). Leave GHub open so you remember to switch back to your normal profile for other sims.",
